      "raw": "[quote=\"Blackfang108\"]\n\n&nbsp;\n<div class=\"bb-quote\"><b>phantaskippy wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class=\"bb-quote-body\">Was the first target you hit with it destroyed? &nbsp;The first target (or last target) you hit would be the one most likely to cause the computer to not process the second hit, because the target didn&#39;t survive the initial hit.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nThe first target was the Operative (I think MAY have been a Corrupt Cop who was killed, can&#39;t remember), who was still in one piece (then.&nbsp; I turned her to paste later).The last target was a mook (not a Corrupt Cop, not a Goons).I&#39;ll see if I can replicate the issue later.\n\n[/quote]\n\nOK, I was able to replicate, eventually.&nbsp;\n\nMy first game, CAR came out after Sparky flipped.&nbsp; The last target (as well as some others) died.&nbsp;I was given the choice of who SkyScraper was to hit. I hit rewind, and tried it again, killing the first target.&nbsp; Still got the choice.\n\nSo I restsarted until I had CAR and Micro-Assembler in hand, so I could make sure to try it with an unflipped Chairman.\n\nOn&nbsp;her second turn, SkyScraper played CAR.\n\nThe first target I hit was an unflipped Chairman, and I did NOT get the option of choosing who SkyScraper was to hit.\n\nI rewound, and hit The Operative first, and was given the choice of who SkyScraper was to hit.\n\nSo it seems that if the very first target doesn&#39;t take damage, Catch A Ride doesn&#39;t trigger.\n",
